-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 9. A Valkey error reply is DATA, and the statement does not raise.
--
-- A helper that raised on WRONGTYPE could not be used to assert that a key
-- holds the wrong type, and the fault suites have to read the keyspace after a
-- fault has fired. The SELECT 1 after each is the assertion that nothing was
-- raised - without it the row above would be indistinguishable from output
-- produced before an error.
